g straight up took over the tva  and made himself the god over  them even b15 when talking to mobius  actually references him  she says does he want us to just let  them all branch  he is king the person in charge of the  tva  and this is why mobius and hunter b15  actually don't remember loki  as i'm sure you recall in the original  tba that we've known this entire time  all of the workers are variants although  they did not know that  they thought that they were created by  the timekeepers specifically to work at  the tva but they were  real people before with real lives but  the tva wiped their memories and made  them believe  what they wanted them to believe this is  the same exact thing happening  this specific king has conquered the tva  become their leader and wiped  everybody's memories and made them  believe what he wants them to believe  this is why they have absolutely no  knowledge of who loki is  they have essentially reverted back to  their old state of being brainwashed tva  agents who know nothing else besides  their life at the tva  although this life is them working for  kang now this  king seems to be the next big bad that  we're going to see in the mcu he  controls the tva which essentially means  he controls all of the branch timelines  now whether or not he chooses to wrap  those up and cut them off is entirely up  in the air right now  mobius states that there were 63 new  branches in one unit alone created and  who knows how many units have been  created and judging by the monitor that  we saw in the tva  i counted at least 15 units that were  created  that is a ton of new branches and hunter  b15 states does he want us to just  let them all branch and the way that she  asks this implies that  yes he does and what is his plan right  now we're  unsure it's going to unravel all  throughout phase four but one thing  is for sure this is going to be a  villain unlike any that we've seen  before  a master of time and one that has a  bunch of different  evil variants of himself the new team of  heroes  definitely have their work cut out for  them and speaking of the avengers and  new heroes having their work cut out for  them  this is all going to lead to the next  avengers in-game  level event actually bigger than an  avengers in-game level event  this is all leading to secret wars in  the secret wars  battle world storyline a bunch of  different universes run  into each other it's kind of what like  nathaniel explained happened  a huge multiversal war all these  universes  collide into one into one place from  there all of the heroes fight all of the  bad guys and there are multiple  different  variants of multiple different heroes  multiple variants of iron man multiple  variants of thor  spider-man you get the picture and this  is what is going to happen  in the mcu unfortunately it's not going  to be happening anytime soon i say we're  probably seven to eight years away from  it happening  huge events like avengers infinity war  and avengers in-game don't just happen  every few years or so unfortunately but  when secret wars finally does come out  we're going to be seeing multiple  versions of the avengers multiple  versions of the x-men the fantastic  four all of the heroes that we love are  going to have variants and all of these  variants are going to come together to  fight  the evil variants this also opens it up  for people like robert downey jr and  black widow to return  chris evans can return as steve rogers  because it will be a different version  x-men from the fox universe could return  as well because this won't undo what has  happened in the past because they are  simply  variants from another universe it's  going to be absolutely  insane and this is exactly what loki  just set up  and speaking of people who have their  work cut out for them dr strange  and spider-man are two of those people  now keep in mind that the writer for the  loki series michael waldron  also wrote doctor strange in 