nd doctor  strange  is in spiderman no way home and alfred  molita and jamie foxx are confirmed to  be in the film as well  both from different universes so  spider-man no way home is going to be  the first film that we actually see  repercussions of what just happened in  the loki finale  loki and sylvie killing he who remains  slash nathaniel richards  created the multiverse now other  variants of  everybody exist and they're going to  continue  to exist there is no longer a tva  focused on killing these branch  timelines and variants  this is how two things happen in  spider-man no way home the first thing  andrew garfield and toby maguire show up  as variants of spider-man  everything in their movies actually  happened they were simply  in other universes and they are variants  of spider-man peter parker  as loki explained variants can be very  similar to one another or  they can be extremely different like one  could be tom hiddleston and the other  could be  an alligator so this is going to bring  toby maguire spider-man and andrew  garfield spider-man  on screen with our tom holland  spider-man the second thing it's going  to do is bring  all of these other villains from  different universes into  our universe and essentially the  multiversal war  will begin in spider-man no way home the  branches are going to start to go into  other branches and variants from one  branch will cross over  into others from there on out enters the  sinister six in our main  timeline alfred molina's doc ock jamie  foxx's electro  willem defoe's green goblin and others  that are rumored to pop up as well  so as you can see the finale of loki  season 1 has huge repercussions going  forward in the mcu  from here on out the mcu is never going  to be the same we are now  officially out of the marvel cinematic  universe and into  the marvel cinematic multiverse and  anything is possible now now as i  mentioned  this is just one breakdown of the many  breakdowns that i'll be doing over